running at the start of this session) and is unrelated to anything in this
run; flagging for the lead as an OBSERVATION, not something this audit
caused. Playwright (chromium-1243, --no-sandbox) scripts written fresh in
scratch `node/` (lib.js, sweep1.js, measure.js, run_measure.js, analyze3.py,
axecheck2.js, point4_5.js, textarea_check.js, wfcollapse.js, rothcheck.js,
findroth2.js) drive real navigation, real keyboard `Tab`, dark via a real
`#theme-toggle`/`#theme-toggle-mobile` click + `page.reload()`.

Real-Tab / real-focus methodology: for the full-page sweep (point 1a), a
bounded real `page.keyboard.press('Tab')` loop from `document.body`,
recording every distinct focused element's computed outline/box-shadow (date
`<input>` sub-fields report the same element+rect on consecutive Tabs — that
repeat is expected, not a wrap-around, so the loop only stops on landing back
on `<body>`). For the per-control pixel measurements (point 1b/2), one real
`page.keyboard.press('Tab')` first (establishes Chromium's keyboard
`:focus-visible` modality for the whole page, confirmed valid technique by
BK3.2's `testmodality.js`), then `el.focus()` per named target — this
matches how a real Tab-produced ring renders, verified because the FIRST
(genuinely real-Tab) elements in the same run render pixel-identically to
the `el.focus()`-driven ones. `major-expenses`: ticked
`#major-expenses-pin-check-header-unmatched` (reveals Apply/Clear) and
opened every `<details>` (`.open = true`); `dashboard`/`major-expenses`
active-preset cases: real `.click()` on a preset button first (dashboard's
preset "active" state is JS-driven inline `style.backgroundColor`, traced by
reading `dashboard.js:368-376` — not executed as a black box: I confirmed
the trace by observing the resulting computed `backgroundColor` after a real
click matches `rgb(79, 70, 229)`, i.e. `bg-accent-strong`'s own value). An
element taller than the viewport (`/transfers` scroll region) needed an
explicit `el.scrollIntoView({block:'start'})` after focus so its top-left
corner, not some scrolled-off point, anchors the screenshot crop.

Pixel methodology (`analyze3.py`): screenshot a 16px-padded crop around the
focused element, then scan OUTWARD from the border edge in up to 4
directions (top/left/bottom/right), sampling ~1px in (inner/white-ring band)
and ~3px in (outer/accent-ring band), and finding the background reference
by scanning outward until two consecutive samples agree (a stability
plateau) — this replaced two cruder first passes that both produced false
readings I caught and fixed before trusting any number: (1) a fixed left-edge
offset bled into a horizontally-adjacent sibling button's own border color
for Restore/Discard; (2) a fixed top-edge offset on `/dashboard`'s "Period
details" summary bled into an amber stale-data banner text line only ~3px
above it (screenshots `debug-crop.png`/`debug-crop2.png` show the banner is
almost flush against the summary — visually confirmed the ring itself IS
clearly visible there, my sampling point was simply wrong). The final
script also rejects a direction that "stabilizes" only because it's clamped
at a crop/viewport boundary (a real bug I hit on the scroll region once its
top-left was pinned to y=0) by preferring directions where inner or outer
differs from the background. Contrast = WCAG relative-luminance ratio,
computed in Python from the sampled RGB triples, not eyeballed.

=== Point 1: full Tab sweep, every unstyled-ring control, both themes ===

`node sweep1.js` — bounded real-Tab walk on all 6 pages × 2 widths (1300,
390) × 2 themes (dark via real toggle+reload) = 24 runs, 683 total recorded
focus stops. Filtering for BK3's exact signature (`outline: solid 2px` +
`box-shadow: rgb(255,255,255) 0 0 0 2px`) found 65 unique selectors that
receive BK3's fallback ring somewhere across the 6 pages (full list in
`sweep1.json`) — includes every attempt-2-named offender:
`#whatif-new-scenario-toggle`, `#add-chain-step-btn`, the projection
Nominal toggle (`[data-display-dollars="nominal"]`), the active
`.date-range-btn` preset (major-expenses) and the dashboard active preset
(JS inline-style, same `rgb(79,70,229)` fill), nav links, `#theme-toggle`,
`#mobile-nav-toggle`, `.major-expense-row-toggle`, Restore/Discard, the
"Period details" `<summary>`, and the `/transfers` scroll region — plus
every other `bg-accent-strong` action button reachable without extra clicks
(`income-sources-list.html`/`expense-sources-list.html` "Add" buttons,
major-expenses "Add" submit).

`node run_measure.js` + `python3 analyze3.py` pixel-measured every one of
those named targets (72 records: 6 scenarios × 2 widths × 2 themes,
`measure-worktree.analyzed3.json`) — filtering to `computed.active===true`
(excludes the desktop-hidden mobile toggle / mobile-hidden nav-link
combinations, which are trivially N/A, not failures) gives 56 real,
applicable readings. **Minimum measured max-of-(inner-vs-bg,
outer-vs-bg) across ALL of them: 5.76:1**, at `light 1300/390 whatif
wf-tab-overview`, `light 390 major-expenses date-range-btn-active`, and
`light 1300/390 insights-june insights-tab-trends` (outer accent-vs-card
ring, `rgb(79,70,229)` vs `rgb(245,245,244)`). Every other reading is
≥6.29:1 (light) or ≥7.61:1 (dark); many are 15–17:1. **No reading is below
3:1 anywhere I measured.** Full table in this verdict's evidence dir
(`report-worktree.txt`) and reproduced for the previously-failing controls:

