**Point 2: FAIL** — the `:where():not([class*="focus-visible:ring"],
[class*="focus:ring"])` exclusion list only recognizes Tailwind RING
utility classes; it does not recognize (a) pre-existing bespoke
attribute-selector focus rules already in the stylesheet
(`[data-wf-tab]`, `[data-ins-tab]`, `[data-wf-collapse-toggle]`,
`[role="region"][tabindex="0"]`, `[data-display-dollars]`,
`[data-projection-compare-toggle]` — all added by an earlier task, BL3),
nor (b) Tailwind's OUTLINE utility family (`focus:outline*`, as opposed to
`focus:ring*`). For the accent-strong-filled members of that set
(projection toggle, roth button, scroll region) the box-shadow ADDITION is
harmless-to-beneficial (matches Point 1's fix). For the two explicitly-named,
already-fine, NOT-accent-strong-filled members (`#wf-tab-overview`,
`#insights-tab-trends`) it is a confirmed, reproducible, dark-mode-visible
deviation from "identical to master" — real, not a screenshot artifact,
literally named in this task's own acceptance text as something that must
NOT happen.

