=== FAILURES ===

1. **This task's own acceptance text, point 2 ("Ring-utility controls
   unchanged vs master... computed outline AND box-shadow identical to
   master") — web/static/css/styles.css (BK3 attempt-3's block) as applied
   to `#wf-tab-overview` (What-If, `web/templates/pages/whatif.html:183`)
   and `#insights-tab-trends` (Insights, `web/templates/pages/
   insights.html:163`), dark theme, both widths.** Both buttons are
   selected by the pre-existing `[data-wf-tab]:focus-visible` /
   `[data-ins-tab]:focus-visible` rule (`styles.css:231-236`, predates this
   task, unchanged) which already gives them a correctly-visible accent
   outline on master — no fix was needed here. Because these buttons carry
   no `focus-visible:ring`/`focus:ring` utility class, BK3's `:not()`
   exclusion (which only recognizes Tailwind ring-utility class substrings)
   does not skip them, so they ALSO now receive BK3's white `box-shadow: 0
   0 0 2px white`, layering a second visible ring band that master does not
   have. Confirmed via direct computed-style diff (master `boxShadow: none`
   vs worktree `boxShadow: rgb(255, 255, 255) 0px 0px 0px 2px`, both
   themes, real Tab) AND visually (`big-master-dark-1300-whatif-wf-tab-
   overview.png` — single thin ring; `big-worktree-dark-1300-whatif-wf-tab-
   overview.png` — visibly wider two-band ring). Not a contrast/WCAG
   violation (ring stays single-hue accent, ≥15:1, arguably MORE visible)
   and imperceptible in light mode (white-on-white), but it is a real,
   reproducible deviation from this task's own explicit "controls with a
   ring utility unchanged vs master" promise for 2 of the 4 named example
   controls — the same CLASS of finding (double indicator via an incomplete
   `:not()` exclusion list) that FAILED attempt 1 (its Finding 2, on
   `[data-kpi-detail]`), now recurring against a DIFFERENT gap in the same
   exclusion mechanism (attribute-selector rules and the `focus:outline*`
   utility family, rather than a missing ring-utility check). The same root
   cause also touches `#wf-collapse-money-toggle` (and by the same
   selector, `#wf-collapse-assumptions-toggle` /
   `#wf-collapse-strategies-toggle`) — not one of the 4 explicitly-named
   controls, included here because it shares the identical mechanism and
   the lead should fix all of them together, not just the two named ones.

